<edge source="iran_hormuz_crisis::maritime_incident_freq" target="alliance_cred_apac::forward_deployment_tempo" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.9</data>
  <data key="d36">An increase in hostile maritime incidents (attacks, seizures, interdictions) prompts alliance members to surge escort, patrol and mine‑countermeasure taskings to protect shipping lanes, raising the tempo of forward deployments.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_hormuz_crisis</data>
  <data key="d39">alliance_cred_apac</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_hormuz_crisis::maritime_incident_freq" target="alliance_cred_apac::naval_platform_availabil" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Sustained higher incident rates drive prolonged deployments and higher operating hours for surface and subsurface units, accelerating maintenance cycles and reducing the stock of immediately available platforms.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_hormuz_crisis</data>
  <data key="d39">alliance_cred_apac</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_hormuz_crisis::maritime_incident_freq" target="china_tech_trade_rivalry::export_goods_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">A rise in hostile maritime incidents around the Strait of Hormuz forces container vessels to reroute, increases transit times and insurance/shipping costs, and causes port and container shortages that immediately reduce the volumetric flow of manufactured exports (including Chinese tech goods) to foreign markets.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_hormuz_crisis</data>
  <data key="d39">china_tech_trade_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_hormuz_crisis::maritime_incident_freq" target="china_tech_trade_rivalry::capital_flow_net" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">An increase in maritime incidents raises sector and route risk premia, prompting portfolio reallocation and slowing foreign direct investment into export‑dependent manufacturing and tech sectors, producing net capital outflows or reduced inflows.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_hormuz_crisis</data>
  <data key="d39">china_tech_trade_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_hormuz_crisis::maritime_incident_freq" target="russia_ukraine_war::long_range_strike_cap" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">A spike in hostile incidents against commercial and naval vessels in the Strait prompts the US/UK and partners to retain or redeploy long‑range munitions, ISR assets and strike‑capable platforms to Gulf contingencies, reducing transfers and operational availability of long‑range strike systems for use in Ukraine.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_hormuz_crisis</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
