<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::defense_supply_levels" target="ai_capital_governance::capital_flow_to_ai" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.65</data>
  <data key="d36">Declining defense inventories prompt governments and institutional investors to reallocate capital toward munitions, logistics and defense tech procurement, crowding out venture and growth funding for non‑defense AI ventures.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_capital_governance</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::defense_supply_levels" target="alliance_cred_apac::operational_sustainabili" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">Diversion of munitions, interceptors and spares to sustain operations in Ukraine reduces inventories available to support prolonged coalition operations in APAC, directly lowering operational sustainability.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">alliance_cred_apac</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::defense_supply_levels" target="china_tech_trade_rivalry::state_export_support_int" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Shortfalls in allied defense supply stocks trigger industrial policy responses—direct subsidies, export financing and diplomatic procurement support—to scale allied production and secure alternative suppliers, increasing state‑level export support focused on strategic industries and allies (and often aimed at reducing dependence on China).</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">china_tech_trade_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::defense_supply_levels" target="iran_hormuz_crisis::diplomatic_engagement_in" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Sustained high Western defense commitments and materiel flows to Ukraine consume political capital and negotiating bandwidth (and reduce available leverage), leading to fewer or less intensive diplomatic mediation efforts focused on the Hormuz crisis.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_hormuz_crisis</data>
</edge>
